cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Kronaxis Polling Method (KPM) in your research, please cite both the published methodology paper and (where relevant) the underlying DYNAMICS-8 framework."
type: software
title: "KPM — Kronaxis Polling Method"
abstract: >-
  Public, falsifiable UK election forecasting with cryptographic
  pre-registration. KPM-v17.10 is a ward-level methodology that combines
  per-ward Uniform National Swing projection with Reform-target detection
  from ONS Census 2021 demographics and Hanretty 2016 Brexit Leave
  estimates, falling back to the hand-crafted KPM-2.2 v15.1 fragmentation
  rule in mid-confidence cases. Every prediction is hashed and committed
  to git before the corresponding election takes place; results are
  auto-scored against actuals; negative findings are reported with the
  same prominence as positive ones.
